menu "Lightbar"

    config LB_REV_NEW
        bool "New PCB revision (EN/INT/PG wired to MCU)"
        default n
        help
            Old PCB3_3 hardwires TPS92390 EN to VDD33, and INT/PG/PD_PG are not
            connected, so the MCU cannot energize or kill the boost stages and
            cannot receive fault interrupts. Enable only on the new revision so
            the code that drives those pins is compiled in. On the new board
            VSENSE_P/N sit across the real sense resistor, so VINOCP becomes a
            critical (gate-closing) fault again.

    config LB_BOOT_SELFTEST
        bool "Run the TPS92390 register selftest at every boot"
        default n
        help
            The selftest rewrites LED_CURR_CONFIG / USER_CONFIG1 / DISPLAY_BRT
            on both drivers. It forces brightness to 0 first and never exceeds
            LB_CODE_MAX, but it still costs ~1 s and is bench diagnostics, not
            production behaviour. Off by default; CLI "m1" runs it on demand.

    config LB_WS2812_ENABLE
        bool "WS2812C status LED fitted"
        default n
        help
            Status LED on LB_WS2812_GPIO. PCB3_3 carries ONE addressable RGB LED
            (LED2: VDD33 / GND / DIN=IO15, DOUT open).

    config LB_WS2812_GPIO
        int "Status LED data GPIO"
        default 15
        depends on LB_WS2812_ENABLE

    config LB_WS2812_COUNT
        int "Status LED count"
        default 1
        depends on LB_WS2812_ENABLE
        help
            PCB3_3 has a single RGB LED. A strip can be attached on the new
            board; set the real pixel count then.

    config LB_WS2812_MAX_BRIGHTNESS
        int "Status LED maximum brightness (0-255)"
        default 96
        depends on LB_WS2812_ENABLE
        help
            Keeps the LED from adding heat/noise next to the analog side.

    config LB_SUN_LAT
        int "Installation latitude, degrees (+N/-S), x10"
        default 470
        help
            Stored x10 to keep Kconfig an integer: 470 = 47.0 deg N. Used by the
            sun-adaptive CCT curve.

    config LB_SUN_LON
        int "Installation longitude, degrees (+E/-W), x10"
        default 80
        help
            Stored x10: 80 = 8.0 deg E. Used for the solar-time correction.

    config LB_SUN_AUTO
        bool "Sun-adaptive CCT follows the sun automatically"
        default n
        help
            When on, the mireds target tracks sun elevation. Off by default so a
            Matter controller keeps full authority over colour temperature. A
            controller writing ColorTemperatureMireds switches it off again.

    config LB_TZ
        string "POSIX TZ string (local time display only)"
        default "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0/2,M10.5.0/3"
        help
            Used only for printing local time. The sun curve works from UTC plus
            longitude, so a wrong TZ never moves the light.

    config LB_OT_TRIP_C
        int "Board over-temperature trip (degC)"
        default 80
        range 40 110
        help
            The SHT40 is placed next to the two TPS92390 on purpose: it measures
            BOARD temperature. When it reaches this value the firmware forces
            both driver outputs off (DISPLAY_BRT=0) and keeps the safety gate
            closed until the board has cooled below the clear threshold for
            several consecutive samples.
            Measured reference on PCB3_3: with 5 V applied and the boost idling
            at 35.5 V (no LED load) the board sits around 59 degC, so the trip
            point has to be comfortably above that.

    config LB_OT_CLEAR_C
        int "Board over-temperature clear (degC)"
        default 68
        range 30 100
        help
            Recovery threshold. Must be below LB_OT_TRIP_C to give hysteresis,
            otherwise a lamp sitting at the limit would switch on and off.

    config LB_STRINGS_PER_CHIP
        int "LED strings connected per driver (1-4)"
        default 3
        range 1 4
        help
            Must match the LED_SET resistor / wiring. Fault bits of unused outputs
            are ignored; the web page shows this many strings per channel.

endmenu
